	(text "POWER – one protected 18650 cell → 5 V for the Pi (Pololu module) and 3.3 V for the radio (MCP1700)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 12.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "21148ef6-3736-520f-b51d-a0e383ec5c01")
	)
	(text "1  CELL, FUSE AND REVERSED-CELL PROTECTION"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ee65e8bc-bb64-5717-ba8b-4c0082f55110")
	)
	(text "What it does, in plain words:\nBT1 - the cell sits in a holder soldered on this board (no battery lead). Use a PROTECTED 18650 (its own\n  protection circuit cuts at a short or a deep discharge). A cable tie through the two board slots next to\n  the holder keeps the cell in during the drop test.\nF1 - a 5x20 mm 4 A fast (F4A) glass fuse in two clips: it blows on a short, and it is pulled out and replaced by hand\n  (keep the spare from the BoM in the box). 4 A: the box draws <= 1.8 A at a nearly empty cell.\nD1 - normally does nothing (it points 'backwards'). If the cell is put in the holder the wrong way round,\n  D1 conducts and shorts it: F1 blows (or the cell's protection cuts) before any module sees -4 V.\n  Bench check: D1's leakage at 4.2 V adds to the standby drain (datasheet up to mA at 40 V and hot;\n  measure the cell current with the box off).\nC1 - 100 uF reservoir at the boost input (Pololu asks for >= 33 uF)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 71.12 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aef1e3ba-5628-566d-b419-ab1c973ae911")
	)
	(text "2  CHARGER LEAD (TP4056 USB-C module at the box wall)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "82d9d7dd-1461-5f98-9258-d348c1089659")
	)
	(text "The TP4056 module (HW-373) sits at the box wall where its USB-C port is reachable; its BAT+/BAT- pads go\nto this 2-pin lead (OUT+/OUT- are not used). It charges the cell at 1 A (about 3.5 h).\nRules: charge with the box switched OFF; use a USB-A-to-USB-C cable (many of these boards lack the\nUSB-C CC resistors, so a C-to-C cable gives no power). J23 is behind F1: a reversed cell never reaches it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 50.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d38366bc-2a48-5f9e-a5c9-c5b5f0fe88c3")
	)
	(text "3  POWER TOGGLE (tells the boost to sleep)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "09eb512e-3986-5ad8-a405-b303e744de2c")
	)
	(text "Toggle CLOSED = ENABLE pulled to GND = boost asleep = box OFF (the battery current never goes through\nthe switch). Toggle OPEN = the module's own 100 k pull-up wakes it = box ON. A lead that breaks in the drop\ntest therefore leaves the box running. Mount the toggle so that 'down' (closed) is marked OFF.\nC18 + R9: 100 nF at the lead, then 1 k to ENABLE: a zap on the lever goes into C18, R9 limits what reaches\nthe module (C18 sits at the connector since checkpoint 3: room on the board). D16: TVS at the lead (after\ncheckpoint 3), P4KE10A, stand-off 8.55 V > the cell's 4.2 V; its leakage (<= 10 uA even at 8.55 V, far less at\n4.2 V) would drop at most 1 V across the 100 k pull-up, so ENABLE still reads high (box ON).\nWith the toggle closed: EN = VBAT x 1k / 101k = 0.04 V (< 0.4 V needed). Off drain: ~40 uA in the pull-up."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 63.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "491cda6e-beaa-519e-85da-78eef7b36bc1")
	)
	(text "4  5 V BOOST MODULE (Pololu U3V70F5)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1b716f14-57e5-5c40-8144-65d569ca1a11")
	)
	(text "This module turns the cell's 3.0-4.2 V into 5.0 V (+-4 %) for the Pi: about 3 A available at a 3.0 V cell,\nthe Pi needs about 1 A at most. Input protected against reversal; below 2.4 V it stops (UVLO).\nENABLE: 100 k pull-up to VIN on the module; < 0.4 V = true shutdown (its output is disconnected).\nKeep the cell -> F1 -> U2 -> GND loop short and wide (1.5-2 mm tracks); keep U2 away from the radio."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7a6b8ac6-6fc8-5ec2-94a0-fdf483c89f39")
	)
	(text "5  ONE-WAY VALVE FOR THE PI'S 5 V (Pololu ideal diode #5388)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 119.38 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "92a3b46f-1ab8-52ad-a331-e7829a97831a")
	)
	(text "U3 lets current flow from the boost to the Pi but never back (< 3 mOhm, so no voltage is lost). If someone\nplugs the Pi's micro-USB while the box is on, the USB supply cannot push current into the boost or the cell.\nIt needs ~3.9 V to start, so it only works on the 5 V side - never on the cell.\nC9 (100 uF) + C10 (100 nF) sit at the box header's pins 2/4: the Pi's supply reservoir.\nRule all the same: do not power the Pi from its micro-USB AND the box at once (two supplies share the Pi)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 177.8 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6d59fae7-db5b-5669-9137-4736b07c269f")
	)
	(text "6  RADIO 3.3 V: MCP1700-3302E/TO from the Pi's 5 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "16ecbb2e-8b1b-53f3-a5f0-5d56cb6abaef")
	)
	(text "A 3-legged regulator: 5 V in, always exactly 3.3 V out for the radio (max 250 mA; the radio takes <= 120 mA).\nFed from 5V_PI, so the radio is only powered when the Pi is: it can never push current into a switched-off\nPi through its pins. 0.2 W at full transmit: warm, not hot. Never feed the radio from the cell or the Pi's\n3.3 V pin (absolute max 3.6 V). C11/C12: 1 uF ceramics (datasheet: >= 1 uF at the output); the breakout\nadds 100 uF + 10 uF + 100 nF at the module. Bench: ripple on 3V3_RADIO during transmit (scope, TP4)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 241.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3f2e3ca9-7ee8-560a-b571-9ec8ed99ebe5")
	)
	(text "7  BATTERY LEVEL (Adafruit MAX17048 #5580, I2C 0x36)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8aff8a40-43f0-572b-9471-5d65b54b2fbc")
	)
	(text "Runs from the cell: its chip (VDD) must sit on BAT through the 3-pad jumper SJ2 (centre pad = VDD, one side VIN,\nthe other BAT). Adafruit says it runs with 3.3 or 5 V on VIN, so it ships VDD-BAT, but the GitHub board\nfile shows SJ2 open (review 24-Oct): ON ARRIVAL check with a meter that SJ2's centre pad connects to BAT;\nif it does not, bridge centre-to-BAT with solder. VIN = the Pi's 3.3 V (3V3_PI, header pin 1): only its\n10 k I2C/INT pull-ups and its LED. BAT / BAT_GND = the JP2 pair, straight at VBAT. INT, QSTART unused:\nthe software polls the gauge over I2C (0x36). Never set MODE.EnSleep in software."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 254 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5ebb362d-fdf8-595b-bd36-713070c4740a")
	)
	(text "8  TEST POINTS (clip a multimeter here)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 287.02 203.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "31698bbc-cc73-5683-ab9a-46c59084c16a")
	)
